[Opening "Nimzo-Indian Defence"]
[Side "black"]
[ECO "E20-E59"]
[Start "d4 Nf6 c4 e6 Nc3 Bb4"]
[Description "Black pins the c3-knight to control e4, often giving the bishop for the knight to double White's pawns. Against the Rubinstein (4.e3), the Classical (4.Qc2), 4.Nf3, 4.f3, 4.Bg5 and the Sämisch (4.a3)."]

